{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final repair report.\n\nProblem: Gerrit 1827 failed because the raw fixture-level batched map was {}, although an immediately following per-event read succeeded in the same repository.\n\nProven root cause: tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py required a one-shot optimization helper to return a complete map even though src/rebar/attest/authorship.py explicitly fails closed to {} on any Git/process/empty-output transient and production callers fall back per event. The deterministic test harness lacked the bounded Git-read recovery already established by tests/_git_counts.py.\n\nProof: deleting the previously implicated 1005 loose blob left both broad and narrow history walks healthy (broad rc=0, 804-byte stdout; narrow rc=0, exact SHA), refuting the prior ENOENT class. Runtime injections of rc128/empty, rc0/empty, and BlockingIOError(EAGAIN) each reproduced the organic sequence: first batched {}, immediate identical replay returns all 8 entries. The same deterministic topology was green in the other CI lanes, ruling out a stable parser/topology defect.\n\nTest: the held-out real-temporary-repository oracle covered all three transient classes plus persistent bounded failure. It was RED first (four failures for missing second attempt/diagnostic), GREEN after the fixer, and returned to four RED failures under the exact omitted-recovery mutation before being restored. The optimization-count sibling test was independently RED with a first-read transient before being wired through the same seam. Refactoring litmus passes: the tests assert exact observable position-to-SHA maps, bounded attempts, and diagnostics, not source text or private implementation structure.\n\nFix: fixture-only `_fixture_batched_map` performs at most five exact resolver attempts, returns on the first complete map, and raises with existing fsck/count-objects/object-listing forensics after persistent failure. Both direct equivalence assertions and the optimization-count production-call-site assertion use it. No src/rebar file changed.\n\nScope and safety: caller sweep found no other direct healthy-fixture assertions outside this module. Production fail-closed/fallback behavior is unchanged; no new capability, dependency, or production semantic change; no existing assertion weakened. The persistent path is finite and louder than before. Construct sibling in the cost assertion was fixed in scope. CLI/MCP/library/automated/dual-direction parity surfaces are N/A because this is a test-harness-only seam. Residual risks: none observed after the in-file sibling sweep.\n\nReplication and gates: focused target 12/12 green; adjacent authorship/compaction/rebuild suites 27/27 green; lint and typecheck green; full local default suite 13,522 passed, 60 skipped, 289 deselected in 2684.33s. Gerrit 1828 earned LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and merged. CI run 31967631562 completed with 17 green jobs; critically, Ubuntu/Python 3.11 (the exact environment that failed 1827) passed.\n\nCI_RESULT: {\"run_id\":\"31967631562\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"duration\":null,\"fixes_applied\":[\"bounded fixture-only recovery and persistent diagnostics\"],\"retry_count\":0}. Commit: 29448f61c095c4f63afb9291ae156a4e0163d843. Gerrit: 1828."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786909921324188001,"uuid":"cc633c19-73ff-41be-9f42-0c89f8729c9e"}